{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"840b031150873bcf","name":"card_unit_p51_b","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_p51_b","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"P-51 B","text":"Destruction: Give your units +2+2 and draw 2 cards.","flavorText":"The P-51B was a single-seat fighter aircraft used by the United States during WWII. It was a variant of the P-51 Mustang, a long-range escort fighter primarily designed to accompany and protect Allied bombers during their missions. The P-51B was introduced in 1943 and featured improvements over its predecessors, including a more powerful Merlin engine which increased its speed and long-range capabilities, making it an effective escort fighter and a formidable opponent for enemy aircraft. The B and C models only had 4x .50 cal guns, but this would be increased to six in the D model line. The long-range capability of the P-51B was due in large part to the addition of external fuel tanks, and this enabled the aircraft to escort bombers deep into enemy territory. A total of 1,987 P-51B’s variants were produced and they remained in service until the end of the war. Quite a few of these variants were operated by the RAF as \"Mustang III\".","faction":"USA","type":"fighter","rarity":"Unique","cost":7,"operationCost":2,"attack":6,"defense":6},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_p51_b","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_p51_b_title","SourceString":"P-51 B","LocalizedString":"P-51 B"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":6,"defense":6,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":7,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_p51_b_text","SourceString":"Destruction: Give your units +2+2 and draw 2 cards.","LocalizedString":"Destruction: Give your units +2+2 and draw 2 cards."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_p51_b_history","SourceString":"The P-51B was a single-seat fighter aircraft used by the United States during WWII. It was a variant of the P-51 Mustang, a long-range escort fighter primarily designed to accompany and protect Allied bombers during their missions. The P-51B was introduced in 1943 and featured improvements over its predecessors, including a more powerful Merlin engine which increased its speed and long-range capabilities, making it an effective escort fighter and a formidable opponent for enemy aircraft. The B and C models only had 4x .50 cal guns, but this would be increased to six in the D model line. The long-range capability of the P-51B was due in large part to the addition of external fuel tanks, and this enabled the aircraft to escort bombers deep into enemy territory. A total of 1,987 P-51B’s variants were produced and they remained in service until the end of the war. Quite a few of these variants were operated by the RAF as \"Mustang III\".","LocalizedString":"The P-51B was a single-seat fighter aircraft used by the United States during WWII. It was a variant of the P-51 Mustang, a long-range escort fighter primarily designed to accompany and protect Allied bombers during their missions. The P-51B was introduced in 1943 and featured improvements over its predecessors, including a more powerful Merlin engine which increased its speed and long-range capabilities, making it an effective escort fighter and a formidable opponent for enemy aircraft. The B and C models only had 4x .50 cal guns, but this would be increased to six in the D model line. The long-range capability of the P-51B was due in large part to the addition of external fuel tanks, and this enabled the aircraft to escort bombers deep into enemy territory. A total of 1,987 P-51B’s variants were produced and they remained in service until the end of the war. Quite a few of these variants were operated by the RAF as \"Mustang III\"."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Destruction"],